  "worked_solution": "The given transformation is a rotation of ${90}^{∘}$ about the origin, which is a rigid motion. Rigid motions preserve the distances between all points and all angle measures. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14214989/assets/9b250f6eda245b8a3530851d21c5438ded3fcbe9ba8cbf6db524a2c2749c3d86.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Under the action of the transformation, the distance between all corresponding points is preserved. Therefore, $BC={B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Under the action of the transformation, the distance between all corresponding points is preserved. Therefore, $AB={A}^{′}{B}^{′}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Under the action of the transformation, the distance between all corresponding points is preserved. Therefore, $CD={C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$\n\nAs a result, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
